 "_doc": "Hair + headwear compatibility, read by src/config/headwearFit.js (read its HAIR + HEADWEAR COMPATIBILITY comment first). Hand-set. `families`: what each headwear family does to the hair FEATURES a scalp mask cannot judge (keep = shown even where the hat's cover hides hair, drawn under the hat so its crown overlaps the base; hide = removed even where nothing else is; cover = follows the hat's cover like the rest of the hair), plus the measured-shape `profile` in headwearFit.json it falls back on. `headwear`: every headwear id (hidden ones too, since wearers still render them) to a family, or {family, ...feature overrides} for the one piece that differs from its family. `hair`: every hairstyle id to a behaviour type, plus `regions` (polygons in ART fractions of the hair image, 0..1 across and down) for the features it has. `sky`: hair may not show above the hat's own underside (hatUndersides.json) in any column the hat occupies, so nothing grows through a brim or out of a crown; kept features are exempt. `pairs`: 'hairId:hatId' overrides, only where no family or item rule can say it.",
